WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.997 --> 00:00:15.082
Oh my God.

00:00:15.499 --> 00:00:17.001
I'm so excited.

00:00:17.376 --> 00:00:18.377
(Applause and cheers)

00:00:19.378 --> 00:00:22.423
This is the first time
I’ve seen people since March 2020.

00:00:22.423 --> 00:00:23.424
Hi!

00:00:23.591 --> 00:00:24.842
Hi, people.

00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:26.635
I’ve had a lot of accomplishments,

00:00:26.635 --> 00:00:29.180
but this is a dream come true right now --

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.181
(Applause and cheers)

00:00:30.181 --> 00:00:31.182
by the way.

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:33.434
So make some noise for the dress.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:35.895
(Applause and cheers)

00:00:35.895 --> 00:00:37.938
And now the back of the dress.

00:00:37.938 --> 00:00:39.398
(Applause and cheers)

00:00:39.398 --> 00:00:41.108
Can we get booty cam, please?

00:00:41.108 --> 00:00:42.109
(Laughter)

00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:43.110
Booty cam!

00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:46.614
If you follow me on social media
you’ve probably seen my heinie before;

00:00:46.614 --> 00:00:47.615
it’s no secret.

00:00:47.615 --> 00:00:48.616
(Cheers)

00:00:48.616 --> 00:00:50.826
But you know, I used to hate my ass ...

00:00:50.826 --> 00:00:51.827
believe it or not.

00:00:52.286 --> 00:00:54.622
I have my father’s shape
and my mother’s size,

00:00:54.622 --> 00:00:56.791
so it was big and long.

00:00:56.999 --> 00:00:58.000
(Laughter)

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:02.129
I used to think that only asses
like J.Lo’s or Beyoncé’s could be famous.

00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:04.048
I never thought that could happen to me.

00:01:04.048 --> 00:01:06.717
I always felt like my body type
wasn’t the right one

00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:08.928
or the desirable one growing up,

00:01:08.928 --> 00:01:12.431
because I grew up in an era
where having a big ass wasn’t mainstream.

00:01:13.182 --> 00:01:15.434
I grew up watching movies
where women were like,

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:17.019
“Does my ass look fat in this?”

00:01:17.019 --> 00:01:18.646
like it was a bad thing.

00:01:18.854 --> 00:01:19.855
(Laughter)

00:01:20.439 --> 00:01:22.733
I felt like the ass odds were against me,

00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:24.026
but baby --

00:01:24.026 --> 00:01:25.111
(Laughs)

00:01:25.111 --> 00:01:28.114
this badonkadonkdonk was going places.

00:01:28.114 --> 00:01:31.784
(Cheers and applause)

00:01:31.826 --> 00:01:33.828
My ass has been the topic of conversation,

00:01:33.828 --> 00:01:35.246
my ass has been in magazines.

00:01:35.246 --> 00:01:37.706
Rihanna gave my ass a standing ovation.

00:01:37.706 --> 00:01:38.707
(Cheers)

00:01:38.707 --> 00:01:40.543
Yes, my booty,

00:01:40.543 --> 00:01:42.711
my least favorite part of my body.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.547
How did this happen?

00:01:45.422 --> 00:01:46.423
Twerkin’.

00:01:46.465 --> 00:01:47.466
(Laughter)

00:01:47.466 --> 00:01:49.218
(Applause and cheers)

00:01:49.426 --> 00:01:51.011
Through the movement of twerking,

00:01:51.011 --> 00:01:53.848
I discovered my ass is my greatest asset.

00:01:53.931 --> 00:01:55.182
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:55.182 --> 00:01:56.725
welcome to TED ...

00:01:56.725 --> 00:01:57.726
Twerk!

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:58.811
(Laughing)

00:01:58.936 --> 00:02:00.437
(Applause and cheers)

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:01.981
I’m going to take my shoes off,

00:02:01.981 --> 00:02:03.065
is that OK with y’all?

00:02:03.065 --> 00:02:04.066
(Cheers)

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:09.321
So the first time I saw twerking in person
was at a teen club called The Z

00:02:09.321 --> 00:02:10.698
in Houston, Texas.

00:02:11.323 --> 00:02:12.533
Hey, shout out, Houston,

00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:13.993
we got some Houstonians here!

00:02:14.577 --> 00:02:18.372
There I saw a bunch of girls my age
shaking their booty to New Orleans bounce,

00:02:18.372 --> 00:02:20.457
and I was like, “How are they doing that?”

00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:22.668
It was incredible to me.

00:02:22.793 --> 00:02:25.504
Thanks to my Caribbean besties,
Peaches and Jolene,

00:02:25.504 --> 00:02:26.714
and thanks to Master P --

00:02:26.714 --> 00:02:28.174
whoop, whoop --

00:02:28.174 --> 00:02:29.300
I found the rhythm.

00:02:30.134 --> 00:02:31.218
The better I got,

00:02:31.218 --> 00:02:33.429
the more I fell in love with what I had,

00:02:33.429 --> 00:02:36.432
because, damn, my ass could do magic.

00:02:37.266 --> 00:02:39.143
Finally, I could twerk,

00:02:39.143 --> 00:02:41.437
but twerking did not begin with me ...

00:02:41.437 --> 00:02:42.438
believe it or not.

00:02:42.438 --> 00:02:43.522
(Laughing)

00:02:43.814 --> 00:02:45.566
I know you think
I invented twerking;

00:02:45.566 --> 00:02:46.567
I didn’t.

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:49.111
I want you to know
where twerking came from.

00:02:49.486 --> 00:02:52.239
I think everyone should know
where everything comes from.

00:02:52.531 --> 00:02:54.992
You should know where
your food and water come from;

00:02:54.992 --> 00:02:57.161
you should know
where your clothes come from.

00:02:57.578 --> 00:03:00.915
It’s important to me to keep
the origin story of twerking alive.

00:03:01.373 --> 00:03:03.959
So here’s some farm-to-table for that ass.

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:05.419
(Laughter)

00:03:05.419 --> 00:03:07.546
(Applause)

00:03:08.214 --> 00:03:11.425
Modern-day twerking derived
from Black people and Black culture.

00:03:11.675 --> 00:03:15.095
It has a direct parallel
to West African dances like mapouka.

00:03:15.679 --> 00:03:18.849
Traditionally, mapouka was a dance
for West African women

00:03:18.849 --> 00:03:21.352
to be used as a celebration of joy,

00:03:21.352 --> 00:03:22.937
religious worship

00:03:22.937 --> 00:03:25.564
or a dance to do at a wedding
to show you were DTF

00:03:25.564 --> 00:03:27.024
or DTM ...

00:03:27.024 --> 00:03:28.692
down to marry, down to marry --

00:03:28.692 --> 00:03:30.110
get your mind out the gutter.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.111
(Laughter)

00:03:31.528 --> 00:03:34.990
Black women carried these dances
across the transatlantic slave trade

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:38.077
to the ring shout and what became
the Black American Church,

00:03:38.077 --> 00:03:41.747
into the hips of Ma Rainey
and Bessie Smith when they sang the blues,

00:03:41.747 --> 00:03:44.458
into the bounce of 
Josephine Baker’s banana dance.

00:03:44.541 --> 00:03:46.418
From jazz dance to jitterbug,

00:03:46.418 --> 00:03:48.629
from shake ya tailfeather
to shake your thang

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:50.297
to that thang thangin.

00:03:50.297 --> 00:03:51.298
(Laughter)

00:03:51.507 --> 00:03:54.760
Black people carried
the origins of this dance through our DNA,

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:55.803
through our blood,

00:03:55.803 --> 00:03:56.887
through our bones.

00:03:56.971 --> 00:04:01.267
We made twerking the global,
cultural phenomenon it has become today.

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.937
Now, as a big, Black woman who has ass,

00:04:04.937 --> 00:04:05.938
who can twerk

00:04:05.938 --> 00:04:07.815
and who’s been doing it her whole life,

00:04:07.815 --> 00:04:10.025
I kind of think I'm an expert
on the subject.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:15.364
I want to add to the classical etymology
of this dance because it matters.

00:04:16.365 --> 00:04:18.742
Black people will not be erased
from the creation,

00:04:18.742 --> 00:04:19.743
the history

00:04:19.743 --> 00:04:21.245
and the innovation of twerking.

00:04:21.245 --> 00:04:22.538
(Applause and cheers)

00:04:22.538 --> 00:04:23.539
Thank you.

00:04:23.539 --> 00:04:24.540
(Applause)

00:04:25.082 --> 00:04:28.002
From TikTok trends to songs and humor,

00:04:28.002 --> 00:04:31.171
we see so much erasure
of what Black people have created,

00:04:31.171 --> 00:04:33.048
so I want to do everything in my power

00:04:33.048 --> 00:04:35.592
to prevent the erasure
of Blackness from twerking.

00:04:36.802 --> 00:04:39.513
Twerking is a Black American
communal collaboration

00:04:39.513 --> 00:04:41.515
born of Black Southern culture.

00:04:41.932 --> 00:04:44.977
From DJ Jubilee and Cash Money
Records in New Orleans,

00:04:44.977 --> 00:04:45.978
to Lil Jon

00:04:45.978 --> 00:04:47.688
and the Ying Yang Twins in Atlanta,

00:04:47.688 --> 00:04:49.315
to Uncle Luke in Miami,

00:04:49.315 --> 00:04:52.776
twerking was alive and well
in nearly every Black club in the South.

00:04:53.319 --> 00:04:55.946
But it would take years
after these songs were released

00:04:55.946 --> 00:04:58.157
for twerking to finally become mainstream.

00:04:59.074 --> 00:05:00.242
I got a test for y’all.

00:05:01.201 --> 00:05:04.204
(Singing) Uh-oh, uh-oh, uh-oh oh, no, no.

00:05:04.204 --> 00:05:06.707
Uh-oh, uh-oh, uh-oh, oh, no, no.

00:05:06.832 --> 00:05:07.833
You know that one?

00:05:07.875 --> 00:05:08.876
Hold up.

00:05:08.917 --> 00:05:09.918
Ya’ll ain’t see it.

00:05:10.919 --> 00:05:15.924
(Singing) Uh-oh, uh-oh, uh-oh oh, no, no,
uh-oh, uh-oh, uh-oh, oh, no, no.

00:05:15.924 --> 00:05:16.925
(Applause and cheers)

00:05:16.925 --> 00:05:18.302
The “Uh-oh” dance.

00:05:18.635 --> 00:05:21.347
Beyoncé called it that
because she was trying to warn us.

00:05:21.347 --> 00:05:22.348
(Laughter)

00:05:22.389 --> 00:05:23.724
Because of Destiny’s Child,

00:05:23.724 --> 00:05:25.684
bootylicious is in the dictionary.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:31.023
And because of Beyoncé’s 2003 music video
for her single “Crazy in Love,”

00:05:31.023 --> 00:05:34.151
the world was introduced
to the “Uh-oh” dance.

00:05:34.777 --> 00:05:38.113
That was the first time I’d ever seen
a popstar do something like that,

00:05:38.113 --> 00:05:39.740
and I wanted to be just like her.

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:43.118
Beyoncé gave me permission
to be myself ...

00:05:43.118 --> 00:05:45.120
to be bootylicious.

00:05:45.579 --> 00:05:48.707
Because she could shake ass
and still be seen as classy

00:05:48.707 --> 00:05:50.125
in the eyes of America.

00:05:50.376 --> 00:05:51.543
And that was hard to do.

00:05:52.086 --> 00:05:55.672
When I moved from Houston
to Minneapolis in the early 2010s,

00:05:55.672 --> 00:05:59.301
I hadn’t seen twerking in a while
until Big Freedia’s tour came to town.

00:05:59.718 --> 00:06:04.223
Now, Big Freedia performs bounce music
with the voice of a preacher

00:06:04.223 --> 00:06:06.225
and the body of bad bitch.

00:06:06.392 --> 00:06:07.393
(Laughter)

00:06:07.393 --> 00:06:09.144
If you can imagine, it’s incredible.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.563
Big Freedia has a moment in her shows

00:06:11.563 --> 00:06:13.690
where she will call people
on stage to twerk,

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:16.527
and she chose me from the audience
to battle another person.

00:06:16.944 --> 00:06:20.864
And I remember being like, 
“Oh my God, I miss this so much.”

00:06:20.948 --> 00:06:21.949
(Laughter)

00:06:22.157 --> 00:06:24.076
When I was up there I thought to myself,

00:06:24.076 --> 00:06:26.078
not only am I shaking ass
but I am winning,

00:06:26.078 --> 00:06:29.248
and besides Big Freedia,
I’m the best twerker in the building.

00:06:29.706 --> 00:06:30.916
And just like that,

00:06:30.916 --> 00:06:32.584
I was reintroduced to twerking.

00:06:33.377 --> 00:06:35.504
When I started to perform my solo music,

00:06:35.504 --> 00:06:38.132
I began incorporating twerking
into my performances,

00:06:38.132 --> 00:06:40.008
and people would go crazy.

00:06:40.592 --> 00:06:42.803
I performed for mainly indie audiences,

00:06:42.803 --> 00:06:45.055
so they didn’t know
what the fuck was happening,

00:06:45.055 --> 00:06:46.223
and I liked it that way.

00:06:46.223 --> 00:06:47.224
(Laughter)

00:06:47.641 --> 00:06:49.393
Twerking made me feel empowered.

00:06:49.977 --> 00:06:51.687
It was my secret language;

00:06:51.687 --> 00:06:52.688
my sauce.

00:06:53.605 --> 00:06:55.858
Little did I know
that a couple of years later,

00:06:55.858 --> 00:06:59.445
Miley Cyrus would perform what seemed
like the twerk heard around the world.

00:07:00.195 --> 00:07:01.321
Y’all remember that.

00:07:02.531 --> 00:07:03.740
In 2013,

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:05.200
within a month of each other,

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.077
I released my debut project,

00:07:07.077 --> 00:07:08.120
“Lizzobangers,”

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.747
and Miley Cyrus released
her project, “Bangerz.”

00:07:11.498 --> 00:07:14.918
That same year, Miley released
the single “We Can’t Stop,”

00:07:14.918 --> 00:07:16.587
and she was twerking in the video.

00:07:17.171 --> 00:07:19.006
I remember being like, “This is crazy;

00:07:19.006 --> 00:07:21.175
Hannah Montana
twerking all over the place.”

00:07:21.175 --> 00:07:22.176
(Laughter)

00:07:23.427 --> 00:07:26.722
A couple months later, she performed
with Robin Thicke on the V.M.A.s,

00:07:26.722 --> 00:07:29.641
and that night, seemingly overnight,
twerking went mainstream.

00:07:30.309 --> 00:07:34.688
The media described twerking as, I quote,
“disturbing and disgusting.”

00:07:35.564 --> 00:07:36.982
Critics blasted twerking

00:07:36.982 --> 00:07:40.110
as something that was exploiting
and over-sexualizing young women.

00:07:40.903 --> 00:07:42.196
Once mainstream,

00:07:42.196 --> 00:07:44.865
twerking was misunderstood
and taken out of context.

00:07:45.824 --> 00:07:46.867
It was bittersweet.

00:07:47.159 --> 00:07:48.327
For one,

00:07:48.327 --> 00:07:51.997
I wish that a Black woman could have
popularized twerking in the mainstream.

00:07:51.997 --> 00:07:53.582
But on the other end,

00:07:53.582 --> 00:07:57.920
twerking going mainstream played a role
in the rise of my profile and my career.

00:07:59.004 --> 00:08:00.005
Listen.

00:08:00.923 --> 00:08:02.716
Everything that Black people create,

00:08:02.716 --> 00:08:05.260
from fashion to music to the way we talk,

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:08.514
is co-opted, appropriated
and taken by pop culture.

00:08:08.514 --> 00:08:13.227
(Applause)

00:08:13.519 --> 00:08:14.520
For this reason,

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:16.188
optimism can be an illusion

00:08:16.188 --> 00:08:18.440
to the experience
of Black people in America.

00:08:19.358 --> 00:08:20.359
In this TED Talk,

00:08:20.359 --> 00:08:22.152
I’m not trying to gatekeep,

00:08:22.152 --> 00:08:25.531
but I’m definitely trying to let you know
who built the damn gate.

00:08:25.531 --> 00:08:26.532
(Laughs)

00:08:26.532 --> 00:08:31.662
(Applause and cheers)

00:08:32.162 --> 00:08:35.415
The fact that I can make a stake
in the reclamation of Black things

00:08:35.415 --> 00:08:36.416
and Black culture

00:08:36.416 --> 00:08:37.876
makes me very optimistic.

00:08:38.585 --> 00:08:42.839
To be on stage at the premiere conference
for the experts in their field,

00:08:42.839 --> 00:08:44.341
talking about twerking --

00:08:44.341 --> 00:08:45.759
(Laughter)

00:08:45.759 --> 00:08:47.594
and stating my facts,

00:08:47.594 --> 00:08:48.845
makes me optimistic.

00:08:49.263 --> 00:08:53.308
The best thing I can do
is be loud and take ownership,

00:08:53.308 --> 00:08:54.768
because for me,

00:08:54.768 --> 00:08:56.603
twerking is a pearl of optimism.

00:08:57.229 --> 00:08:59.898
It’s a form of self-expression, freedom --

00:08:59.898 --> 00:09:01.233
confidence.

00:09:01.441 --> 00:09:03.569
Twerking is not
just something I do to music.

00:09:03.569 --> 00:09:05.153
It’s extremely useful.

00:09:05.571 --> 00:09:08.574
It manifests in my life
in ways that I need more joy.

00:09:08.574 --> 00:09:09.783
In the mornings,

00:09:09.783 --> 00:09:12.578
twerking leads me to stretching
and taking care of my body.

00:09:12.578 --> 00:09:14.329
I bend over and I isolate my cheeks;

00:09:14.329 --> 00:09:15.497
I’m in downward dog.

00:09:15.497 --> 00:09:16.832
(Laughter and cheers)

00:09:16.832 --> 00:09:17.833
Namaste.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.586
(Laughter)

00:09:22.129 --> 00:09:24.256
Sometimes I’ll put on a song
and I shake ass,

00:09:24.256 --> 00:09:26.174
and immediately I’m in love with myself.

00:09:26.174 --> 00:09:27.342
And not just self-love.

00:09:27.342 --> 00:09:28.552
I mean like,

00:09:28.552 --> 00:09:30.137
“OK, Lizzo, what’s your number?”

00:09:30.137 --> 00:09:31.138
(Laughter)

00:09:31.305 --> 00:09:32.431
I would do me.

00:09:32.514 --> 00:09:34.349
But it’s not just sexual.

00:09:34.641 --> 00:09:35.851
(Laughter)

00:09:35.976 --> 00:09:37.102
It's not.

00:09:37.227 --> 00:09:40.480
(Applause and cheers)

00:09:41.189 --> 00:09:44.568
Twerking is a deep,
soulful, spiritual practice.

00:09:44.568 --> 00:09:45.611
It’s hip-opening.

00:09:46.111 --> 00:09:47.195
It’s empowering.

00:09:47.738 --> 00:09:49.239
When performed as the mapouka,

00:09:49.239 --> 00:09:51.033
it’s said to connect you to God.

00:09:51.366 --> 00:09:52.367
It’s sacred.

00:09:52.743 --> 00:09:55.495
And now we’re practicing
that on mainstream stages.

00:09:55.871 --> 00:09:58.290
We're practicing that at home,

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:02.336
and it's contributing to the liberation
of women and people around the world.

00:10:02.878 --> 00:10:04.379
Twerking is good for humanity.

00:10:04.838 --> 00:10:06.173
(Laughter)

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:08.675
Forty years ago,

00:10:08.675 --> 00:10:11.678
when Black and brown people in New York
invented break dancing,

00:10:11.678 --> 00:10:12.888
it was villainized.

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:17.434
Mainstream media weaponized break dancing
by connecting it to gang activity

00:10:17.434 --> 00:10:18.435
and violence.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:20.270
As an art form and subculture,

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:21.605
it wasn’t taken seriously.

00:10:22.689 --> 00:10:23.982
Fast-forward to today,

00:10:23.982 --> 00:10:25.901
break dancing is now an Olympic sport.

00:10:27.402 --> 00:10:29.196
What will be the future of twerking?

00:10:30.238 --> 00:10:32.074
Russian ballet dancers are twerking.

00:10:32.449 --> 00:10:33.450
Have you seen it?

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:34.451
They  be like this.

00:10:35.952 --> 00:10:37.162
Y’all think I’m playing.

00:10:37.162 --> 00:10:38.372
They’re out there like --

00:10:38.372 --> 00:10:39.623
(Singing) Doo doo doo doo.

00:10:39.623 --> 00:10:41.500
(Laughter)

00:10:41.833 --> 00:10:43.293
Can we clear Tchaikovsky?

00:10:43.377 --> 00:10:44.378
(Laughter)

00:10:46.254 --> 00:10:48.924
Will we see twerking
as an Olympic sport one day?

00:10:50.133 --> 00:10:52.135
And will Black people still be part of it?

00:10:53.553 --> 00:10:55.472
I’m proud to be a twerk pioneer.

00:10:56.056 --> 00:10:58.475
I’m grateful for the asses
that came before me.

00:10:58.934 --> 00:10:59.976
